# PreparedWeights-1: prepared rank folders of the BUILT weights, and the stored startup estimate (TF_GLM_PREPARED_DIR;
# default unset = today's path).
# Upstream: jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark patches/0140-glm-fast-boot.patch (Apache-2.0), as adapted by lanes
# BootDeepseek / BootFable2 (scripts/glm53/v110/lanes/BootFable2/ots0105-glm-fastboot-prepared-folders.patch), ported
# to the synced tree. Changes from ots0105: the knob TF_GLM_PREPARED_DIR; TF_GLM_EXPERT_ROTATE in the key; a whole-file
# code hash of every module the build executes (shares.py, kernels/qmm.py, direct_read.py and the package __init__
# added), gated by a trace and an environment recording in the test; the index and tokenizer hashed by content; weight
# files by name, size and mtime; a self-checksummed manifest; fsynced data, manifest and directories; a per-rank flock
# so the next write removes a killed writer's leftover; every chunk verified by default.
# Rank 0's weights.load is 47.5-50.4 s of a boot (median 76 s, run-20261029-185803, "weights: 53.6 GB on the GPU"); a
# folder reads back at the reader's 4.0-4.4 GB/s, measured on GB10 (lanes/BootFable2 fastboot_rt.py, full verify):
# ~12-13 s. Disk: ~50-57 GiB per rank per key; KEEP = 2 keys per rank.
# Startup estimate (lane BootGaps' finding): capacity.admit's checkpoint pass parses all 46 headers (112,727 tensors)
# and runs GLM's transform on each: 1.4-1.5 s on the laptop, run on every rank before the load. GlmEngine passes admit an
# ``estimate`` hook. fastboot.cached_estimate stores the pass's three integers under the weights key plus the vision flag
# and the code of engine.py, capacity.py and geometry.py, and reads them back in ~17 ms (laptop). capacity.admit's new
# ``estimate`` argument defaults to None (the pass as before) for every other family.
# Files: tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/fastboot.py, weights.py, engine.py (one keyword argument at the admit call),
# tensorfold/cuda/capacity.py (the optional hook). Applies with patch -p0 from the directory holding tensorfold/, to
# stack/all and to the plain synced tree. Tests: test_prepared_weights.py, test_estimate.py.
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/fastboot.py
