+Boot timeline: ``mark(phase)`` prints one ``[boot]`` line a phase on every rank with the seconds since the launch, the
+phase's own seconds (since the previous mark) and the memory state, so a restart's phases stop being inferred from
+the gaps between unrelated log lines. The launch time is TF_GLM_LAUNCH_T0 or TF_GLM_T0 (epoch seconds, set by a
+launcher) when given, else this module's import.
+
+Prepared folders (TF_GLM_PREPARED_DIR; jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark 0140, Apache-2.0, as adapted by lanes
+BootDeepseek and BootFable2, ported to the synced tree): rank 0's ``weights.load`` takes 47.5-50.4 s of a boot whose
+median is 76 s (the run-20261029 boot logs: "weights: 53.6 GB on the GPU (48.5s)"). It is not disk-bound: it splits
+this rank's share out of every checkpoint tensor, EXL3-unpacks the routed experts, MSE-quantizes the dense matrices
+to 4 bits and stacks and uploads each layer, the same bits every time. This module stores what the loader BUILT (every
+tensor's storage bytes, dtype, shape, stride and offset, and the objects around them) in one folder a rank::
+
+    $TF_GLM_PREPARED_DIR/<model>/<key hash>/rank<R>/{manifest.json,data.bin}
+
+and the next start reads it back with no conversion at all. The key covers everything that decides a built byte:
+the checkpoint (every weight file's name, size and mtime; config.json, tokenizer.json and the index by content), the
+rank, the tensor-parallel world, the MTP flag, the build knobs (``KNOBS``), torch's and numpy's versions, the device
+type and the source of every module the build runs (``WEIGHT_CODE``, whole files). A folder whose key differs, whose
+manifest fails its own checksum, whose data file has the wrong size or whose chunks fail their SHA-256 is never
+served: the checkpoint path runs instead (fail-safe, never fail-open).
+
+Written only when TF_GLM_PREPARED_WRITE=1 on a start that had to build (or offline: ``python -m <this module>
+prepare``), into a sibling temporary folder renamed into place after the data and the manifest are on disk, under a
+per-rank lock; a killed or failed write leaves no folder at the key's path, and the next write removes the leftover.
+
+Reader: 64 MiB chunks, several threads, O_DIRECT where the file system takes it (the page cache is the GPU's memory
+on GB10), pinned double buffers and async device copies on a stream per thread. TF_GLM_PREPARED_VERIFY=full (the
+default) checks every chunk's SHA-256, ``sample`` every 16th and the last, ``off`` none.
+
+No torch at import: the key, manifest and folder logic run in host-only tests.
